## A

### Action

Use “action” for what Home Assistant is asked to do. Older guidance says “service”: these mean the same thing. A request to run an action does not prove the device finished it.

### App

Use “app” for software that runs alongside Home Assistant on Home Assistant OS. Older instructions and some saved files say “add-on”. Say “app (previously add-on)” once. An app is not an integration, a dashboard card or the Companion app on a phone.

### Area

A room or other space that groups devices and entities. An area is not a zone. Acting on an area may change several entities.

### Assist

Home Assistant’s voice and text assistant. A helpful reply does not prove the right device was controlled.

### Attribute

Extra information about an entity, such as brightness. Write the attribute name in code formatting only when someone must copy it. An attribute is not the state.

## B

### Blueprint

A reusable pattern for making an automation or script. Choosing inputs or saving a blueprint-based automation does not mean it has run.

## C

### Card

A block on a dashboard. Do not use “widget” or “tile” unless that is the card’s name.

### Condition

A check that decides whether a run carries on. A condition does not start a run and does not wait until it becomes true.

## D

### Dashboard

A set of views and cards for checking or controlling the home. A dashboard being hidden does not stop anyone reaching a device.

### Device

A physical product or a service that groups several entities. One device may have many entities, and some entities have no device.

### Device class

A more specific kind of entity, such as a door or a temperature sensor. Write it in lower case, as a label, not as a state.

### Domain

The first part of an entity ID: in `light.reading_lamp` the domain is `light`. It is not an internet domain.

## E

### Entity

One reading, control or function in Home Assistant, such as a lamp or a temperature. An entity is not always a physical device. Say “light”, “sensor” or “switch” when you can.

### Entity ID

Write “entity ID”, not “entity id” or “identifier”. The format is `domain.object_id`, all lower case, with underscores. Changing the name of an entity does not necessarily change its ID.

### Event

A message that something happened. Receiving one does not prove a device did something.

## F

### Floor

A group of areas on one level. Do not infer a building layout from it.

## H

### Helper

A stored value or simple calculation, such as a toggle or a counter. Editing a draft helper does not change anything until it is saved.

## I

### Integration

The connection between Home Assistant and a device family or service. Not the same as an app.

## L

### Label

A tag you can put on many things to organise or target them. A label is not a room.

## P

### Person

A Home Assistant person entity, which combines phones and other trackers. It is not a user account. It does not prove where a person is.

## S

### Scene

A saved set of device states you can request together. A scene is not a timed routine. Activating it does not prove every device reached its state.

### Script

A sequence of actions you start yourself or from an automation. Saving a script does not run it. Stopping a script does not undo what it already requested.

### State

The value Home Assistant holds for an entity. It is not necessarily a fresh reading or what a person asked for.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| The light is off. | The light reports Off. |

#### Unavailable and unknown

“Unavailable” means Home Assistant cannot get the state now. “Unknown” means no usable state has been supplied. Neither means 0, and neither proves the device is offline. See [States, requests and errors](../writing-guidelines/states-and-errors.html).

## T

### Template

A way to calculate or format a value. A template result is not a measured value. A missing input must not become 0.

### Trigger

What starts an automation. Saving or turning on an automation is not a trigger.

## Y

### YAML

The text format used for some configuration. Keep spacing, keys and quotation marks exactly.

## Z

### Zone

A place on a map used for location features. A zone is not a room.

